WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.660
♪

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:43.600
♪

00:00:43.600 --> 00:01:10.220
♪

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:32.620
♪

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:55.240
♪

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:56.240
Five.

00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:07.920
♪

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:08.920
Ten.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:22.600
♪

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:25.600
Fifteen.

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:27.600
No!

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:51.960
♪

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:58.960
Anybody home?

00:02:58.960 --> 00:02:59.960
Mr. Graff?

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:00.960
Mr. Graff?

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:28.960
Mr. Graff?

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:51.960
♪

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:53.960
Are you all right?

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:57.960
He's coming around now.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:58.960
Who are you?

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:00.960
How do you feel?

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:04.960
Rotten.

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:05.960
Who are you?

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:06.960
You'd better relax, mister.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:08.960
You've had a nasty blow on the head.

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:10.960
This is Mr. Ridley.

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:12.960
Charlie Ridley.

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:14.960
My name is Malamose.

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:16.960
We're friends of Mr. Graff's.

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:18.960
Who hit me?

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:20.960
Don't you know?

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:22.960
Who are you out here with?

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:25.960
I came out here alone to see Mr. Graff.

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:40.960
Graff?

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:44.960
That body was warm when I got here.

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:46.960
It's 1.30 now.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:47.960
When did you get here?

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:48.960
About noon, I guess.

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:50.960
That's when my appointment was.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:51.960
Appointment?

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:53.960
Yes, Graff telephoned me and asked me to come out here.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.960
He said he had something he wanted me to take care of.

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:56.960
Can you prove it?

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:02.960
He had it written down on his desk bed.

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:06.960
Gone.

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:09.960
Something else is gone, too.

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:11.960
You mean the diamonds?

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:13.960
That's exactly what I mean.

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:15.960
We found them.

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:16.960
We phoned the police.

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:17.960
They should be here soon.

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:19.960
They should have been here sooner.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:21.960
That fact doesn't seem to disturb you.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:22.960
You mean about the police?

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:25.960
Why should it?

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:27.960
You mean you think I killed this man?

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:28.960
Not necessarily.

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:30.960
It could have been your partner.

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:31.960
My partner?

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:33.960
Sure.

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:36.960
After all, I doubt that you hit yourself on the head.

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:40.960
He left you to face the music alone.

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:43.960
Why shield him?

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:44.960
Who is he?

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:46.960
You're crazy.

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:48.960
The police will certainly be curious.

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:50.960
That's what they get paid for, but why are you curious?

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:52.960
And who did you say you were?

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:53.960
This is Mr. Malinus.

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:54.960
My name is Ridley.

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:56.960
I still want to know who you are.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:01.960
What my colleague is trying to say is that we're business associates of Mr. Graff.

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:03.960
Partners.

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:05.960
We're importers of gems.

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:07.960
Precious stones.

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:12.960
Whoever tried to steal those diamonds from Graff was stealing from us, too.

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:16.960
Naturally, we're kind of anxious to find out who's behind all this.

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:18.960
I see.

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:20.960
So I'm a killer and a thief.

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:22.960
Is that the picture you're going to paint for the police?

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:25.960
How do you sketch yourselves into this little scene?

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:29.960
We arrived after the murder, and we can prove it.

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:32.960
Who put you up to this, Barnett?

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:34.960
I found this in your pocket.

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:36.960
Your name's in it.

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:38.960
Private investigator, huh?

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:44.960
That's a detective who enforces a law of supply and demand, Charlie.

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:48.960
None of them will do anything for money.

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:50.960
Did you get paid a lot for this job, Barnett?

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:55.960
Not that it's any of your business, but the job I came out here to do is to pick up some valuables from Graff

00:06:55.960 --> 00:06:58.960
and take them to a lockbox in New York City.

00:06:58.960 --> 00:06:59.960
He hired me on the telephone.

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:01.960
He didn't tell me what the valuables were.

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:03.960
I presume they were diamonds.

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:06.960
And thanks very much for picking me up off the floor.

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:09.960
Oh, your money's all there.

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:13.960
We retained everything that was yours.

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:17.960
What do you mean by that?

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:19.960
Just this.

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:20.960
The diamonds.

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:22.960
We told you.

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:26.960
We found them in your pocket.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:31.960
Now I begin to get the picture and the frame that goes with it.

00:07:31.960 --> 00:07:34.960
Nobody framed you, Barnett.

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:38.960
We're businessmen, not bandits.

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:41.960
We happen to think somebody put you up to this.

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:45.960
If you won't tell us, you'll very soon tell the police when they get here.

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:47.960
When are the police getting here?

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:48.960
They're due here any minute.

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:50.960
We phoned them half an hour ago.

00:07:50.960 --> 00:07:52.960
You phoned them on that phone?

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:54.960
Naturally.

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:55.960
We'd better call them again.

00:07:55.960 --> 00:07:58.960
I think you were disconnected.

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:03.960
You boys had better splice that thing together and call your lawyers.

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:04.960
I'll get the cops.

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:07.960
Barnett!

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:11.960
What'd you say your business was, importing precious stones?

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:13.960
That's right.

00:08:13.960 --> 00:08:15.960
You're also cop shy.

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:19.960
When do you do your importing, on dark nights and on deserted beaches?

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:23.960
The customs people call it smuggling.

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:27.960
We call it keeping the overhead down.

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:39.960
Barnett, take a look out that back window.

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:42.960
The two platoon system, huh?

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:44.960
What do those two pirates do, bury the loot?

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:45.960
Not the loot.

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:47.960
The general manager.

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:49.960
They're digging a grave, Barnett.

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:51.960
Big enough for two.

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:53.960
Why don't you cooperate?

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:54.960
What do you want to know?

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:57.960
Graff bought 15 diamonds today.

00:08:57.960 --> 00:08:59.960
Eight of them were found in your pocket.

00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:03.960
Who were you out here with and where are the other seven diamonds?

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:07.960
If I don't tell you, I go through that door, is that it?

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:08.960
It's up to you.

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:12.960
And if I do tell you, you let me leave through that door?

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:16.960
After all, we can't afford to turn you over to the police.

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:20.960
That's not exactly an answer, but then I'm not going to give you one either.

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:22.960
You're making a big mistake, Barnett.

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:25.960
You help us, we let you off the hook.

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:27.960
Why should you?

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:31.960
If I'm legitimate as I say I am, I'd go straight to the police.

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:36.960
If I'm a thief as you say I am, I'd blackmail you, try to cut my son.

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:37.960
Uh-huh.

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:41.960
If I talk, you'll have to pull that trigger.

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:44.960
Well, she's all dug and I'm beat.

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:45.960
Did he open up yet?

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:49.960
He has a foolish notion the longer he keeps us guessing, the longer he lives.

00:09:49.960 --> 00:09:51.960
Yeah?

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:52.960
That's a mistake.

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:54.960
Meet the rest of the firm.

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:56.960
Mr. Lekin, Mr. Sallow.

00:09:56.960 --> 00:10:00.960
We better hurry up and get that stiff in the ground before we have to bury him sitting up.

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:01.960
It's getting late.

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:04.960
You better finish the job.

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:05.960
I mean...

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:07.960
Suppose you finish it, Pudgy.

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:09.960
You and that other straw boss.

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:13.960
Graff's ain't been dead a couple hours yet and everybody's giving orders.

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:15.960
I broke my back digging that hole out there.

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:18.960
Suppose you break yours dragging that tub of lard out there and throwing him in it.

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:20.960
Sure, sure, Barnett.

00:10:20.960 --> 00:10:22.960
Will somebody keep him covered?

00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:23.960
I got him.

00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:24.960
Take a seat, Lillie.

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:25.960
Yeah, sure.

00:10:25.960 --> 00:10:27.960
Oh, uh...

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:33.960
Couldn't we finish this little matter first and then just fill in the hole?

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:35.960
You mean let the coolies do it, huh?

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:36.960
What's the matter?

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:39.960
You afraid the detective will talk to us while you're gone?

00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:41.960
Yeah, well, maybe he will.

00:10:41.960 --> 00:10:43.960
We trust you, Barney.

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:45.960
Why should you?

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:47.960
Let me see those diamonds.

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:48.960
Why?

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:49.960
Come on!

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:50.960
You're right.

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:51.960
Got them right here.

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:54.960
I see you have all eight of them.

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:56.960
We'll start being partners.

00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:58.960
I'll take my two right now.

00:10:58.960 --> 00:10:59.960
I'll just take any two.

00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:00.960
Okay.

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:03.960
I'll take mine.

00:11:03.960 --> 00:11:07.960
There you are, Sam.

00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:09.960
Don't fill in that hole.

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:13.960
Leave plenty of room on top.

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:15.960
Okay, Mr. Detective.

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:20.960
Now you and me are gonna talk my language.

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:24.960
Let me.

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:28.960
You know, Sal, this guy's got plenty of moxie.

00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:30.960
We could use a little of that in our outfit.

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:31.960
What, him?

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:32.960
He's a thief!

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:34.960
Oh, who ain't?

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:36.960
There, you can keep him covered.

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:38.960
Him and me is gonna have a little talk.

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:41.960
Come here, Barnett.

00:11:41.960 --> 00:11:42.960
Sit down.

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:43.960
Look.

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:46.960
How'd you like to join our organization, huh?

00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:48.960
Well, now, I've been waiting for an offer.

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:50.960
All I've had is threats.

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:51.960
It's a lead pipe.

00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:53.960
We're salesmen, that's all.

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:56.960
We just wait for the goods to come in, split it up,

00:11:56.960 --> 00:11:58.960
and we each got a territory.

00:11:58.960 --> 00:11:59.960
Sounds all right.

00:11:59.960 --> 00:12:01.960
How does the goods get in?

00:12:01.960 --> 00:12:02.960
Risk, you mean?

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:03.960
No risk.

00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:06.960
We got a guy working the boats, a sailor.

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:09.960
He picks up the diamonds on the other side.

00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:12.960
They're usually hot stuff, so he gets them cheap.

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:14.960
He sneaks them in.

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:16.960
How?

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:18.960
How?

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:19.960
Who knows?

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:21.960
In the captain's ears.

00:12:21.960 --> 00:12:23.960
Anyhow, he brings them in, see?

00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:25.960
Takes them out in the mud, buries them.

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:26.960
Then we go clamming.

00:12:26.960 --> 00:12:28.960
We all go clamming, tell him.

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:31.960
Yeah, well, Sal means that Graft doubled on us

00:12:31.960 --> 00:12:33.960
and went out by himself.

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:34.960
He'd made a side deal, see?

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:36.960
Didn't tell the organization.

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:38.960
But we heard about it.

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:40.960
That's why we all come out here today.

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:41.960
That's how we found you.

00:12:41.960 --> 00:12:42.960
Yeah.

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:45.960
Wasn't that a lucky thing for you, I mean, huh?

00:12:45.960 --> 00:12:47.960
Getting in on a setup like this.

00:12:47.960 --> 00:12:49.960
Yeah, just what I've always wanted.

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:52.960
The only thing is, we stand to lose a lot of dough.

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:55.960
The whole organization does, including you.

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:59.960
You see, seven of the diamonds are still missing, partner.

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:01.960
Where are they?

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:03.960
You mean you want me to tell you, too?

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:06.960
Oh, what do you mean, tell me, too?

00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:08.960
Who else did you tell?

00:13:08.960 --> 00:13:09.960
Animals?

00:13:09.960 --> 00:13:11.960
Why, they're...

00:13:11.960 --> 00:13:13.960
Ah, he said you didn't talk.

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:15.960
Yeah, that's what he said.

00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:17.960
Get Malamose.

00:13:17.960 --> 00:13:19.960
We're gonna have a showdown right now.

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:23.960
All right, let's have it.

00:13:23.960 --> 00:13:25.960
What's all this about a showdown?

00:13:25.960 --> 00:13:26.960
What's going on here?

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:28.960
What went on, you mean?

00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:31.960
You tell Sal and me to go out there and dig a hole in the sand.

00:13:31.960 --> 00:13:33.960
You guys go through him like a loose leaf notebook.

00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:34.960
That's how it was, huh?

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:36.960
What are you talking about?

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:37.960
He didn't tell us anything.

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:38.960
I'll bet.

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:41.960
Now listen, pudgy boys, I've been double dealt once today.

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:42.960
I ain't gonna be twice.

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:43.960
You're crazy.

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:46.960
Barnack told you where the diamonds were, didn't he?

00:13:46.960 --> 00:13:47.960
He did not.

00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:48.960
Hey!

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:55.960
Hey, sit down.

00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:57.960
He didn't tell us.

00:13:57.960 --> 00:13:58.960
Did he tell you?

00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:00.960
No wonder you're giving me orders.

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:01.960
You're richer than I am, huh?

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:02.960
Don't holler at me.

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:05.960
I got no more of an idea where those diamonds are than you do.

00:14:05.960 --> 00:14:06.960
Or maybe you do.

00:14:06.960 --> 00:14:07.960
Oh, take it easy, you fool.

00:14:07.960 --> 00:14:08.960
What did you do, beat it out of him?

00:14:08.960 --> 00:14:09.960
Why, you...

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:10.960
Stop it, I said!

00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:12.960
Stop it, you hear?

00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:15.960
Don't you see what he's trying to do?

00:14:15.960 --> 00:14:16.960
You bet I do.

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:18.960
No, no, no.

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:20.960
I mean Barnett.

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:22.960
He started all this.

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:23.960
Don't you see?

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:26.960
He hasn't told anybody.

00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:28.960
He has no intention of talking.

00:14:28.960 --> 00:14:33.960
He's gonna try to angle through this alive so that he can get to the diamonds.

00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:34.960
Yeah.

00:14:34.960 --> 00:14:36.960
That's right.

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:39.960
You made another mistake, Mr. Barnett.

00:14:39.960 --> 00:14:41.960
It was worth a try.

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:43.960
You might have all shot each other.

00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:45.960
Are you gonna tell us who's got those diamonds?

00:14:45.960 --> 00:14:47.960
What's your hurry?

00:14:47.960 --> 00:14:50.960
We don't have much time, and you have even less.

00:14:50.960 --> 00:14:52.960
Maybe he's stalling because he doesn't know.

00:14:52.960 --> 00:14:55.960
Maybe he's on the level and someone tried to frame him.

00:14:55.960 --> 00:14:56.960
Maybe you're right.

00:14:56.960 --> 00:14:58.960
If he is legit, what'll we do with him?

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:01.960
Stand him up against that wall.

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:04.960
Come on, you.

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:06.960
Hey, listen.

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:09.960
If we do it here, we gotta lug this guy outside.

00:15:09.960 --> 00:15:11.960
He ain't no bag of butterflies.

00:15:11.960 --> 00:15:12.960
Sure.

00:15:12.960 --> 00:15:14.960
We take him outside.

00:15:14.960 --> 00:15:15.960
Then he just falls in the hole.

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:17.960
Nobody has to lug him.

00:15:17.960 --> 00:15:18.960
Lazy.

00:15:18.960 --> 00:15:19.960
Oh, boy.

00:15:19.960 --> 00:15:22.960
Take him outside.

00:15:22.960 --> 00:15:35.960
Come on.

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:36.960
This is a duplex.

00:15:36.960 --> 00:15:37.960
You can move right in.

00:15:37.960 --> 00:15:39.960
Well, he says he's ready.

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:41.960
Go ahead, Salo.

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:42.960
What do you mean?

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:43.960
Me?

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:44.960
You've got a gun, haven't you?

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:45.960
So what?

00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:46.960
So have you.

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:47.960
Go ahead.

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:48.960
Shoot.

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:49.960
You know what, Sal?

00:15:49.960 --> 00:15:51.960
I think the pudgy boys are afraid of a murder rap.

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:52.960
But on us, it's all right.

00:15:52.960 --> 00:15:53.960
Yeah.

00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:54.960
All right, come on.

00:15:54.960 --> 00:15:55.960
We'll all do it.

00:15:55.960 --> 00:15:56.960
Come here.

00:15:56.960 --> 00:15:57.960
Come here.

00:15:57.960 --> 00:15:58.960
I'll show you.

00:15:58.960 --> 00:16:01.960
Now, turn around, you.

00:16:01.960 --> 00:16:03.960
Here's what we do.

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:05.960
I'll empty the cylinder.

00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:07.960
Put one cartridge back in the chamber.

00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:15.960
We'll all take turns in the trigger till Mr. Barnett joins our friend, Mr. Graff.

00:16:15.960 --> 00:16:16.960
Russian roulette.

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:19.960
Barnett, you're gonna like this.

00:16:19.960 --> 00:16:21.960
I'd rather play run, sheep, run.

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:22.960
Try it.

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:28.960
Since you say you don't know anything about the diamonds, let's not waste any more time, huh?

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:33.960
I'm aiming right at your head, squeezing the trigger.

00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:35.960
Well, what do you know about that?

00:16:35.960 --> 00:16:37.960
It hit an empty chamber.

00:16:37.960 --> 00:16:39.960
Your turn, Mr. Lackin.

00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:41.960
Yeah.

00:16:41.960 --> 00:16:43.960
Okay.

00:16:43.960 --> 00:16:48.960
Right between the shoulders.

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:49.960
What do you know?

00:16:49.960 --> 00:16:52.960
I just swore there's a bullet in there somewhere.

00:16:52.960 --> 00:16:53.960
Your turn, Ridley.

00:16:53.960 --> 00:16:54.960
Why, this is murder.

00:16:54.960 --> 00:16:55.960
I don't...

00:16:55.960 --> 00:16:58.960
You hadn't intended to do any of your own killing, is that it?

00:16:58.960 --> 00:17:03.960
You better do it, Ridley.

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:06.960
You got a lot of luck, Mr. Barnett.

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:09.960
Your turn, Sallow.

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:15.960
Oh, Sallow's a type that likes to shoot from the hip, a method that's not very accurate.

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:17.960
All he may do is wound you.

00:17:17.960 --> 00:17:22.960
We hate to have to bury a wise who is just painfully wounded.

00:17:22.960 --> 00:17:24.960
Hope you're having fun.

00:17:24.960 --> 00:17:25.960
Why not?

00:17:25.960 --> 00:17:26.960
You've had yours.

00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:28.960
We're entitled to ours sometime.

00:17:28.960 --> 00:17:30.960
A few laughs, a few diamonds.

00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:32.960
The odds are right, mister.

00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:33.960
One to three.

00:17:33.960 --> 00:17:34.960
That's a short price.

00:17:34.960 --> 00:17:38.960
Go ahead, Sallow.

00:17:38.960 --> 00:17:41.960
What remarkable luck you've had, Mr. Barnett.

00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:43.960
It's my turn again.

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:45.960
Shall I take it?

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:47.960
What do you hope to prove?

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:51.960
First, if there's really a bullet in here.

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:54.960
Second, that you remember where the diamonds are.

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:56.960
What makes you think I'd tell you even if I knew?

00:17:56.960 --> 00:17:59.960
It's coming back to him now, but Barney has another turn.

00:17:59.960 --> 00:18:01.960
There's only one left.

00:18:01.960 --> 00:18:02.960
Hear that, detective?

00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:05.960
There's only one chamber that hasn't been fired.

00:18:05.960 --> 00:18:07.960
I hear it.

00:18:07.960 --> 00:18:11.960
Apparently, you do think we're bluffing, huh?

00:18:11.960 --> 00:18:12.960
But are you sure?

00:18:12.960 --> 00:18:13.960
I'm sure you're crazy.

00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:17.960
Are you sure there's not a bullet in that chamber?

00:18:17.960 --> 00:18:19.960
All right, Barney.

00:18:19.960 --> 00:18:20.960
I had my turn.

00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:21.960
You take it.

00:18:21.960 --> 00:18:22.960
Thanks, pal.

00:18:22.960 --> 00:18:23.960
So have I.

00:18:23.960 --> 00:18:24.960
There, this was your idea.

00:18:24.960 --> 00:18:25.960
Hear that, Barnett?

00:18:25.960 --> 00:18:27.960
It's my turn again.

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:29.960
I'm ready.

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:31.960
Are you?

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:32.960
Okay, Malamus, you win.

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:34.960
I think you're crazy enough to do it.

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:36.960
I'll tell you where the diamonds are.

00:18:36.960 --> 00:18:37.960
He's lying, Alex.

00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:38.960
Hold it, hold it.

00:18:38.960 --> 00:18:39.960
Wait a minute.

00:18:39.960 --> 00:18:40.960
There's a boat out there.

00:18:40.960 --> 00:18:41.960
Come on, let's get in the house.

00:18:41.960 --> 00:18:47.960
You said you knew where the diamonds were.

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:48.960
Did I?

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:51.960
I meant I know who has them.

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:52.960
Who?

00:18:52.960 --> 00:18:54.960
One of you four.

00:18:54.960 --> 00:18:56.960
Oh, that's not smart.

00:18:56.960 --> 00:18:59.960
You're the only ones who knew Graff was going to pick them up today.

00:18:59.960 --> 00:19:00.960
Very clever.

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:02.960
Come on, let's knock this guy off right now.

00:19:02.960 --> 00:19:03.960
Wait a minute.

00:19:03.960 --> 00:19:04.960
Wait a minute.

00:19:04.960 --> 00:19:05.960
Who was it?

00:19:05.960 --> 00:19:08.960
Whoever's most anxious to kill me before I tell his name.

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:10.960
I want to know who it was, too.

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:14.960
Graff was killed about noon, just before I got here.

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:15.960
I have an idea.

00:19:15.960 --> 00:19:18.960
One of you left here just before I arrived.

00:19:18.960 --> 00:19:20.960
I got news for you.

00:19:20.960 --> 00:19:23.960
We all left New York separately.

00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:27.960
We arranged to meet at a gas station about a half a mile down the road.

00:19:27.960 --> 00:19:30.960
Then we all came out together.

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:33.960
We all arrived at the same time.

00:19:33.960 --> 00:19:36.960
Did you all arrive at the gas station at the same time?

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:38.960
Just about.

00:19:38.960 --> 00:19:40.960
I saw Bonnie and Sallow on the road.

00:19:40.960 --> 00:19:42.960
Followed the men.

00:19:42.960 --> 00:19:44.960
They were in the same car.

00:19:44.960 --> 00:19:45.960
That's right.

00:19:45.960 --> 00:19:48.960
And Ridley was waiting for us at the gas station when we got there.

00:19:48.960 --> 00:19:50.960
Oh?

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:52.960
How long had you been waiting, Ridley?

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:55.960
Long enough to have my oil changed.

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:58.960
Who does this egg think he is?

00:19:58.960 --> 00:19:59.960
Well, answer the man.

00:19:59.960 --> 00:20:01.960
How long were you there?

00:20:01.960 --> 00:20:03.960
I told you.

00:20:03.960 --> 00:20:06.960
I got there ahead of you about an hour.

00:20:06.960 --> 00:20:09.960
I had Ben change my oil while I waited for you.

00:20:09.960 --> 00:20:13.960
I never left that station until you arrived.

00:20:13.960 --> 00:20:16.960
We could call Ben at the station.

00:20:16.960 --> 00:20:17.960
Ask him.

00:20:17.960 --> 00:20:18.960
He knows us.

00:20:18.960 --> 00:20:19.960
Phone's out of order.

00:20:19.960 --> 00:20:20.960
One of us could go down there and ask him.

00:20:20.960 --> 00:20:22.960
Yes, and I'll go with him.

00:20:22.960 --> 00:20:24.960
Who's going to stay here with the detective?

00:20:24.960 --> 00:20:26.960
Oh, I'll be all right.

00:20:26.960 --> 00:20:28.960
But there's just one thing.

00:20:28.960 --> 00:20:31.960
If the one who goes to the gas station happens to have the diamonds,

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:34.960
he may never come back.

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:36.960
Why don't we all go?

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:39.960
Take the smart detective with us.

00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:40.960
Are you nuts?

00:20:40.960 --> 00:20:41.960
Why not?

00:20:41.960 --> 00:20:43.960
He knows what'll happen if he tries to step out of line.

00:20:43.960 --> 00:20:44.960
Okay.

00:20:44.960 --> 00:20:45.960
I don't trust any of you.

00:20:45.960 --> 00:20:47.960
I'm glad we'll use Ridley's car.

00:20:47.960 --> 00:20:51.960
Your grave's already dug, mister.

00:20:51.960 --> 00:20:52.960
Tell him, Ben.

00:20:52.960 --> 00:20:54.960
I had the oil changed while I was waiting.

00:20:54.960 --> 00:20:55.960
That's right.

00:20:55.960 --> 00:20:57.960
Mr. Ridley got here a little bit after 11.

00:20:57.960 --> 00:21:00.960
I know because he worked on his car for half an hour,

00:21:00.960 --> 00:21:03.960
changed the oil and like that, and then he went to lunch.

00:21:03.960 --> 00:21:05.960
Oh, he was going at 11.30, regular.

00:21:05.960 --> 00:21:08.960
State Highway Diner, just up the road a piece.

00:21:08.960 --> 00:21:10.960
Was Mr. Ridley here when you left?

00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:11.960
Yep.

00:21:11.960 --> 00:21:12.960
Still here when I got back.

00:21:12.960 --> 00:21:16.960
Said something about waiting for you fellas going up to Mr. Graff's place.

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:17.960
May I ask something?

00:21:17.960 --> 00:21:18.960
Sure thing.

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:20.960
This is your car, isn't it, Ridley?

00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:22.960
That's right.

00:21:22.960 --> 00:21:25.960
When you changed the oil on this car, did you make a record of the mileage?

00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:30.960
Sure, right here.

00:21:30.960 --> 00:21:33.960
Right here.

00:21:33.960 --> 00:21:35.960
36.506.

00:21:35.960 --> 00:21:38.960
It was a half mile to the house after he picked you boys up

00:21:38.960 --> 00:21:40.960
and a half mile back here just now.

00:21:40.960 --> 00:21:43.960
What's the speedometer read?

00:21:43.960 --> 00:21:44.960
36.507.

00:21:44.960 --> 00:21:49.960
And if I did take that extra trip you mentioned while Ben was at lunch,

00:21:49.960 --> 00:21:50.960
what would it read?

00:21:50.960 --> 00:21:53.960
Half mile here and back, 36.508.

00:21:53.960 --> 00:21:55.960
Doesn't show it.

00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:57.960
I think we'd better be heading back, Mr. Barnett.

00:21:57.960 --> 00:21:59.960
Just a minute.

00:21:59.960 --> 00:22:01.960
Could that speedometer have been tampered with?

00:22:01.960 --> 00:22:08.960
I'll look.

00:22:08.960 --> 00:22:10.960
Nope, seal's unbroken.

00:22:10.960 --> 00:22:11.960
Mind if I have a look?

00:22:11.960 --> 00:22:17.960
Nope.

00:22:17.960 --> 00:22:19.960
Well?

00:22:19.960 --> 00:22:20.960
It hasn't been touched.

00:22:20.960 --> 00:22:21.960
That's what it said.

00:22:21.960 --> 00:22:28.960
Shall we?

00:22:28.960 --> 00:22:30.960
Hey, Mr. Malamose.

00:22:30.960 --> 00:22:32.960
I thought you might like to know,

00:22:32.960 --> 00:22:35.960
when that fella had his head under the dashboard there with me,

00:22:35.960 --> 00:22:42.960
he whispered something about me calling the police.

00:22:42.960 --> 00:22:44.960
What fella did you say?

00:22:44.960 --> 00:23:09.960
I don't know. I never even seen him.

00:23:09.960 --> 00:23:11.960
All right, we've got some unfinished business.

00:23:11.960 --> 00:23:12.960
So have I.

00:23:12.960 --> 00:23:14.960
You had your chance, detective. You didn't prove a thing.

00:23:14.960 --> 00:23:15.960
I was stalling for time, Len,

00:23:15.960 --> 00:23:17.960
but now I know who killed Graff and who took the diamond.

00:23:17.960 --> 00:23:20.960
Yeah, yeah, you said that before.

00:23:20.960 --> 00:23:22.960
Now I'll prove it to you.

00:23:22.960 --> 00:23:23.960
Get that driver's seat.

00:23:23.960 --> 00:23:24.960
What?

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:25.960
Go ahead, get in the car.

00:23:25.960 --> 00:23:26.960
Huh?

00:23:26.960 --> 00:23:44.960
Put it in reverse and back around that big tree.

00:23:44.960 --> 00:23:45.960
Okay.

00:23:45.960 --> 00:23:48.960
What is that, Drew?

00:23:48.960 --> 00:23:51.960
Turn around.

00:23:51.960 --> 00:23:53.960
What's that mark on the back of your jacket?

00:23:53.960 --> 00:23:56.960
That's a streak of grease from leaning out the car door.

00:23:56.960 --> 00:23:58.960
That's the easiest way to steer when you're driving in reverse, isn't it?

00:23:58.960 --> 00:23:59.960
Yeah, sure.

00:23:59.960 --> 00:24:02.960
And driving in reverse doesn't register on the speedometer, does it?

00:24:02.960 --> 00:24:04.960
No, it doesn't.

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:06.960
Ridley, what's on the back of your jacket?

00:24:06.960 --> 00:24:07.960
Nothing.

00:24:07.960 --> 00:24:10.960
You got that grease mark driving that extra mile in reverse,

00:24:10.960 --> 00:24:13.960
the one that didn't show on the speedometer while Ben was out to lunch.

00:24:13.960 --> 00:24:15.960
Are you going to believe him?

00:24:15.960 --> 00:24:16.960
Why, he's only driving...

00:24:16.960 --> 00:24:20.960
You search the car, I'll search him.

00:24:20.960 --> 00:24:22.960
Now it's your turn.

00:24:22.960 --> 00:24:25.960
You only put one bullet in there, remember?

00:24:25.960 --> 00:24:26.960
I'll kill you.

00:24:26.960 --> 00:24:28.960
Put up your hands.

00:24:28.960 --> 00:24:31.960
Boy, am I glad to see you.

00:24:31.960 --> 00:24:33.960
Well, how'd you happen to be over in this neighborhood?

00:24:33.960 --> 00:24:38.960
Well, the game warden reported that the owner of this place was out there clamming this morning.

00:24:38.960 --> 00:24:39.960
Came out to serve my summons.

00:24:39.960 --> 00:24:41.960
You know, this whole shore has been posted.

00:24:41.960 --> 00:24:43.960
They're seeding it with oysters.

00:24:43.960 --> 00:24:46.960
You'll have to serve your summons at the grave, I'm afraid.

00:24:46.960 --> 00:24:47.960
Yeah, I saw it.

00:24:47.960 --> 00:24:50.960
Okay, Mac, cover him.

00:24:50.960 --> 00:24:51.960
Is that the killer?

00:24:51.960 --> 00:24:58.960
Yeah.

00:24:58.960 --> 00:25:04.960
Now, we were searching the place just now when the car drove up with the guns on you.

00:25:04.960 --> 00:25:06.960
Is he dead?

00:25:06.960 --> 00:25:09.960
No.

00:25:09.960 --> 00:25:12.960
But I don't think he'll live to walk the last mile.

00:25:12.960 --> 00:25:22.960
He just drove it in reverse.

00:25:42.960 --> 00:25:47.960
